Author-Name: FUJITA, Masahisa
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Pennsylvania
Author-Name: THISSE, Jacques-François
Author-Email: jacques.thisse@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium
Title: Technological linkages and efficient location of indivisible activities: Koopmans-Beckmann and Von Thünen unified
Abstract: Consider a model à la Koopmans-Beckmann involving two indivisible and interactive firms, as well as a continuum of workers. Firm 1 uses labor, while firm 2 uses labor and good 1 produced by firm 1; both goods 1 and 2 can be exported their output but good 1 cannot be imported. The land capitalization process, based on workers' competition on a perfectly competitive land market, is used to design a noncooperative game betwccn firms 1 and 2. The equilibria of this game always exist and are socially optimal. Various extensions of the basic model are also discussed.
