Author-Name: d ASPREMONT, Claude
Author-Email: claude.daspremont@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE and Département des Sciences Economiques, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium
Author-Name: GERARD-VARET, Louis-André
Author-Workplace-Name: G.R.E.Q.E., Ecole des Hautes Etudes en Sciences Sociales, Marseille, France
Title: Moral Hazard in Teams and Repeated Partnership : The Role of Information Quality
Abstract: We analyse the sharing of an uncertain joint output among risk-neutral members of a team whose actions are not observable. Adapting techniques used to treat the pure adverse selection problem to this team moral hazard problem, we define a first condition that is sufficient to implement a first best joint action and a second condition that is sufficient to implement. any joint action . These conditions hold generically. Finally we show ttw usefulness of such eonditions in repeated partnership with imperfect monitoring and prove a folk-theorem.
