Author-Workplace-Name: Department of Economics, V.P.I& S.U, Blacksburg, Virginia 24061, USA
Title: The Value of Failure
Abstract: This simple patent race model distinguishes between technological success and economic success in a fum's research project. It is shown that under certain conditions a researching firm can be technologically unsuccessful and economically successful.
Classification-JEL: O30
Keywords: preexisting results on failed experiments, patent race
