Author-Name: VAN ZANDT , Timothy
Author-Email: tvz@princeton.edu
Author-Workplace-Name: Department of Economics, Princeton University, Princeton NJ 08544 USA
Title: Hidden Information Acquisition and Static Choice
Abstract: This note explores the consequence of hidden information acquisition for static decision theory. \Ve show that any choice correspondence in the observable problem can be consistent with some well-behaved choice correspondence in an unobservable metaproblem with costly information acquisition. This illustrates how choices may not satisfy standard assumptions because a decision maker's decision process (in this case, information acquisition) depends on her choice set. It also illustrates the importance of modeling the source of violations of standard assumptions, rather than simply weakening axioms on preferences.
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1994017
Creation-Date: 1994-03-31
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1994.html
File-Format: text/html
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:1994017

