Author-Name: CABALLERO-SANZ, Francisco
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Valencia and Commission of the European Communities, Directorate General for Competition
Author-Name: MONER-COLONQUES, Rafael
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium 
Author-Name: SEMPERE-MONERRIS, J.J.
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE and IRES Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium 
Title: Optimal Licensing in a Spatial Model
Abstract: This paper studies, in a spatial model. optimal licensing policies by first, comparing our results with the standard (non-spatial) licensing literature, and second, how results are affected if the patent holder can introduce a vertical restraint (exclusive territories). Contrary to standard results we find that royalties are superior to fees. Once the licensor introduces an ET clause, his profits are higher than when he uses either fees or royalties only. A conflict between private and social interests arises since consumers are better off when the technology is licensed via fees.
Keywords: licensing, royalties, fees, exclusive territories
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1994031
Creation-Date: 1994-07-01
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1994.html
File-Format: text/html
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:1994031

