Author-Name: GERARD-VARET, Louis-André
Author-Workplace-Name: G.R.E.Q.A.M., Ecole des Hautes Etudes en Sciences Sociales, Marseille
Title: Moral Hazard in Teams with Uncertainty, and Transfers or Repetition as Enforcement Mechanisms
Abstract: Properties of stochastic outcome functions are exploited to solve the moral hazard problem in teams under unobservable individual actions and different individual objectives. Two kinds of enforcement mechanisms are considered: Enforcement through utility transfers and enforcement through repetition. For both more general results are obtained by adapting conditions previously derived to ensure truthful revelation of private information for collective deciSion-making. These conditions are shown to be generic. Also, one of these being weaker than the condition of pairwise identifiability used by Fudenberg, Levine and Maskin, a new Folk theorem is obtained.
Classification-JEL: D2, D7
Keywords: Mechanism design, team moral hazard, folk theorem
