Author-Name: EECKHOUDT, Louis
Author-Workplace-Name: Catholic Faculties of Mons and Lille
Author-Name: ZENOU, Yves
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium and ERMES, Université Panthéon-Assas
Title: Bid Rents under Unemployment Risk : Delayed versus Timeless Uncertainty
Abstract: In this paper, we analyze the impact of uncertainty on the level and properties of the bid rent function. We show that these properties strongly depend upon the way in which uncertainty is introduced into the model (delayed versus timeless uncertainty). We also investigate the implication of income uncertainty for the city equilibrium.
