Author-Name: GHOSAL, Sayantan
Author-Workplace-Name: Department of Economics, Queen Mary and Westfield College, University of
Author-Name: POLEMARCHAKIS , Heracles
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium
Title: Nash-Walras equilibria
Abstract: At a Nash - Walras equilibrium, individuals exchange commodities competitively, and, simultaneously, they interact strategically. Under standard assumptions, NashWalras equilibria exist, equilibrium profiles of actions are, typically, determinate but Pareto suboptimal, though not constrained Pareto suboptimal: a transfer of revenue need not suffice for a Pareto improvement in welfare.
Classification-JEL: D70, D72, D50, D60
Keywords: Nash, Walras, equilibrium, determinacy, optimality
