Author-Name: MINELLI, Enrico
Author-Workplace-Name: Universita di Brescia and CORE, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium
Author-Name: POLEMARCHAKIS , Heracles
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium
Title: Information at a Competitive Equilibrium
Abstract: Asymmetric information concerns either commodities or mutually exclusive states of the world. The notion of competitive equilibrium differs between the two cases. In particular, incentive compatibility constraints are only relevant in the case of asymmetric information concerning mutually exclusive states of the world, where it is important whether trades are enforceable and whether trades occur before or after individuals receive private information. In either case, competitive equilibria exist under standard assumptions; they may be determinate, but fail to satisfy a notion of Pareto optimality.
Classification-JEL: D50
Keywords: asymmetric information, competitive equilibrium
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1995083
Creation-Date: 1995-12-01
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1995.html
File-Format: text/html
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:1995083

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: POLEMARCHAKIS, Heracles
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium
Author-Name: SALTO, Matteo
Author-Workplace-Name: CORE, Université catholique de Louvain, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium
Title: Balance of payments and determinacy
Abstract: In economies of overlapping generations, competitive equilibrium allocations and interest rates may be indeterminate. In a world economy with multiple countries, a competitive equilibrium need not satisfy the condition that the balance of payments be in equilibrium. In a stationary economy with heterogeneous countries, the requirement that, in addition to market clearing, a balance of payments equilibrium condition be satisfied restores the determinacy of equilibrium; and it may select the monetary steady - state equilibrium.
Classification-JEL: D50, F41
Keywords: balance of payments; determinacy of competitive equilibrium
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1995084
Creation-Date: 1995-12-01
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1995.html
File-Format: text/html
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:1995084

