Author-Name: WILSON, Paul W.
Author-Email: wilson@eco.utexas.edu
Author-Workplace-Name: Department of Economics, University of Texas
Title: Some problems with the Ferrier/Hirschberg bootstrap idea
Abstract: This paper demonstrates that the bootstrap procedure suggested by Ferrier and Hirschberg (1997) gives inconsistent estimates. A very simple example is given to illustrate the statis- tical issues underlying nonparametric efficiency measurement and the problems with the Fer- rier/Hirschberg approach, and may serve as a primer on bootstrapping in nonparametric models of production processes.
