Title: A Bayesian approach to the econometrics of first-price auctions 
Abstract: We propose a Bayesian approach to empirical auction models. We argue that the Bayesian paradigm is more suitable to the study of empirical strategic models than its frequentist counterpart. We perform an estimation of our model on an auction of hand-made miniature sculptures organized by Christie's in London.
Classification-JEL: D44, C11, C15
Keywords: ﬁrst-price auction, private values, Bayesian inference, Gibbs sampling. 
