Title: Repeated games played by cryptographically sophisticated players
Abstract: We explore the consequences of the assumptions used in modern cryptographywhen applied to repeated games with public communication. Technically speaking, we model agents by polynomial Turing machinesand assume the existence of a trapdoor function. Under these conditions, we prove a Folk Theorem in which the minmax level of players has to be taken in correlated strategies instead of mixed strategies..
Classification-JEL: C72
Keywords: repeated games, bounded rationality, correlation, Turing machines, cryptography
