Author-Name: DREZE, Jacques
Author-Email: jacques.dreze@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain (UCL). Center for Operations Research and Econometrics (CORE)
Title: On the dynamics of supply-constrained equilibria.
Abstract: The paper defines a simple tatonnement process of adjustments in prices and quantities, where excess demand results in nominal price increases and excess supply results in quantity rationing of supply at unchanged prices. Under reasonable assumptions, the process converges to a supply-constrained equilibrium. The result contributes to our understanding of how supply-constrained equilibria come about.
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1999004
Creation-Date: 1999-01-01
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1999.html
File-Format: text/html
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:1999004

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: KOUTSOUGERAS, Leonidas C.
Author-Workplace-Name: School of Economic Studies, University of Manchester and Department of Econometrics, Tilburg University
Title: A remark on the number of trading posts in strategic market games
Abstract: In market games the one to one correspondence between commodity types and trading posts would be justified if it were true that the set of equilibria is not affected by the number of trading posts postulated at the outset of the model. We show that this is not true. We develop an example which features equilibria where a commodity is simultaneously exchanged in two trading posts at different prices, i.e., equilibria where the 'law of one price' fails when the one to one correspondence between commodities and trading posts is abandoned. Thus, we conclude that the set of equilibria in market games depends non-trivially on the number of trading posts. This conclusion further suggests that an explanation of the structure of trading posts is necessary.
Classification-JEL: C72
Keywords: trading posts, law of one price. 
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1999005
Creation-Date: 1999-01-19
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1999.html
