Author-Name: DE SINOPOLI, Francesco
Author-Workplace-Name: Center for Operations Research and Econometrics (CORE), Université catholique de Louvain (UCL), 1348 Louvain la Neuve, Belgium
Title: Further remarks on strategic stability in plurality games
Abstract: In this note we show that, for generic plurality games (i.e., voting games under plurality rule), an equilibrium that induces a mixed distribution over the outcomes (i.e., with two or more candidates elected with positive probability), is regular and, hence, a Mertens' stable set. Furthermore, we show that stronger equilibrium concepts, than stability, do not guarantee the existence of a solution for some generic plurality games. A final example shows the weakness of the simple sophisticated voting principle.
Classification-JEL: C72, D72 
Keywords: Plurality rule, regular equilibria, sophisticated voting, stable sets
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1999030
Creation-Date: 1999-05-01
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1999.html
File-Format: text/html
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:1999030

