Title: The identification of preferences from the equilibrium prices of commodities and assets
Abstract: The competitive equilibrium correspondence, which associates equilibrium prices of commodities and assets with allocations of endowments, identifies the preferences and beliefs of individuals; this is the case even if the asset market is incomplete.
Keywords: equilibrium, identiﬁcation
