Author-Workplace-Name: Center for Operations Research and Econometrics (CORE), Université catholique de Louvain (UCL), Louvain la Neuve, Belgium
Title: Approximate edge splitting
Abstract: We show that, in any undirected graph, splitting off can be performed while preserving all cuts of value at most 4/3 times the minimum value, and this is best possible. This generalizes a classical splitting-off result of Lovasz.
