Author-Name: GOURIEROUX, Christian
Author-Workplace-Name: CREST and CEPREMAP
Author-Name: SCAILLET, Olivier
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain (UCL), Louvain la Neuve, Belgium
Title: Bartlett identities tests
Abstract: In this note we propose a general testing procedure for parametric models based on Bartlett Identities. A well-known example is the Information Matrix test, which is based on the Bartlett Identity of order 1. The Identities are shown to induce a sequenceof testable restrictions on the data generating process. When all the restrictions are considered jointly, they are often complete, in the sense that they are satisfied if and only if the model is correctly specified. We show that this is the case for normal, exponential and Poisson models. A test of the joint validity of an arbitrarily chosen subset of restrictions is proposed, and its first order asymptotic properties are presented. An interpretation of the test as a score test for neglected parameter heterogeneity is also given.
Classification-JEL: C12, C52
Keywords: Bartlett Identities, information matrix test, speciﬁcation test
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1999039
Creation-Date: 1999-06-01
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1999.html
File-Format: text/html
