Author-Workplace-Name: Indian Statistical Institute, New Delhi, India
Author-Name: SEN, Arunava
Author-Workplace-Name: Indian Statistical Institute, New Delhi, India
Title: Dictatorial domains
Abstract: In this paper, we introduce the notion of a linked domain and prove that a non-manipulable social choice function defined on such a domain must be dictatorial. This result not only generalizes the Gibbard-Satterthwaite Theorem but also demonstrates that the equivalence between dictatorship and non-manipulability is far more robust than suggested by that theorem. We provide an application of this result in a particular model of voting. We also provide a necessary condition for a domain to be dictatorial and characterize dictatorial domains in the cases where the number of alternatives is three and four.
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 1999040
Creation-Date: 1999-07-05
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp1999.html
File-Format: text/html
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:1999040

