Author-Name: SANIN, Maria Eugenia
Author-Name: ZANAJ, Skerdilajda
Author-Email: skerdilajda.zanaj@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain (UCL). Center for Operations Research and Econometrics (CORE)
Title: Clean technology adoption and its influence on tradeable emission permit prices.
Abstract: In this paper we give an example in which the price of tradeable emission permits increases despite firms' adoption of a less polluting technology. This is in contrast with Montero (2002) and Parry (1998), among others. If two Counot players switch to a cleaner technology, the price for permits may increase due to an increase in the net demand for permits and a decrease in net supply of permits after the clean technology is adopted. This is only the case when output demand is elastic.
Classification-JEL: D43, L13, Q55
Keywords: environmental innovation, tradable emission permits, Cournot interaction
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 2009029
Creation-Date: 2009-04-01
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp2009.html
