Title: How lotteries outperform auctions for charity
Abstract: In their recent paper Goeree et al. (2005) determine that all-pay auctions are better for fundraising activities than lotteries. We show that the introduction of asymmetry among valuations with complete information could reverse this result. Complete information seems well suited to some charity environments.
Classification-JEL: D44, D62, D64
Keywords: all-pay auctions, charity, complete information, lotteries
