Author-Name: LEROUX, Marie-Louise
Author-Email: marie-louise.leroux@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain (UCL). Center for Operations Research and Econometrics (CORE)
Title: On the fiscal treatment of life expectancy related choices
Abstract: In an overlapping generations economy setup we show that, if individuals can improve their life expectancy by exerting some effort, costly in terms of either resources or utility, the competitive equilibrium steady state differs from the ﬁrst best steady state. This is due to the fact that under perfect competition individuals fail to anticipate the impact of their longevity-enhancing effort on the return of their annuitized savings. We identify the policy instruments required to implement the ﬁrst-best into a competitive equilibrium and show that they are speciﬁc to the form, whether utility or resources, that the effort takes.
Classification-JEL: H21, D91
Keywords: life expectancy, health expenditures, taxation
