Title: Announcement wars as an equilibrium selection device
Abstract: This paper attempts to give a rationale to public announcements, so often observed in the real world, and to formalize the idea that they can be used as a form of equilibrium selection device when multiple equilibria arise. It also shows how announcements solve the problems of coordination failures as predicted by the empirical literature based on experimental studies
Classification-JEL: C72, C78, D61
Keywords: multiple Nash equilibria, coordination failure, cheap talk, policy games, announcement equilibrium
