Author-Name: THISSE, Jean - François
Author-Email: jacques.thisse@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, CORE, B-1348 Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium; Paris School of Economics and CEPR
Title: Geographical economics : A historical perspective
Abstract: This paper provides a bird-eye overview of the history of spatial economic theory. It is organized around three main ideas (and authors): (i) land use and urban economics (Thünen), (ii) the nature of competition across space (Hotelling), and (iii) new economic geography and the emergence of economic agglomerations (Krugman).
Keywords: urban economics, spatial competition, economic geography
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 2011012
Creation-Date: 2011-02-01
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp2011.html
File-Format: application/pdf
