Author-Email: filippo.calciano@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, CORE, Belgium and Department of Economics, University of Rome 3, Italy
Title: Oligopolistic competition with general complementarities
Abstract: In this paper we extend the basic model of Cournot competition to the case where both the demand function and the cost functions of each firm depend on the amounts produced by competitors. In this modified setting, proving existence of equilibria becomes harder. We develop a generalization of the theory of supermodular games in the context where individual decision variables take values in a totally ordered set to prove existence of equilibria in this generalized Cournot setting.
Classification-JEL: C60, C70, C72
Keywords: Cournot oligopoly, complementarity, generalized modularity, generalized increasing differences, supermodular games
