Author-Workplace-Name: Georgia Institute of Technology, Atlanta, USA
Title: Finding the stationary states of Markov chains by iterative methods
Abstract: In this paper, we develop new methods for approximating dominant eigenvector of column-stochastic matrices. We analyze the Google matrix, and present an averaging scheme with linear rate of convergence in terms of 1-norm distance. For extending this convergence result onto general case, we assume existence of a positive row in the matrix. Our new numerical scheme, the Reduced Power Method (RPM), can be seen as a proper averaging of the power iterates of a reduced stochastic matrix. We analyze also the usual Power Method (PM) and obtain convenient conditions for its linear rate of convergence with respect to 1-norm.
Keywords: google problem, page rank, power method, stochastic matrices, global rate of convergence, gradient methods, strong convexity, general norms
