Author-Workplace-Name: CREPP, University of Liège; Université catholique de Louvain, CORE, Belgium
Title: Social security and economic integration
Abstract: The purpose of this letter is to analyze the impact of economic integration when countries differ in their social security systems, more specifically in the degree of funding of their pensions, and in the regulation of the retirement age. Funding and mandatory early retirement are two features which foster capital accumulation relative to pay-as-you-go pensions with flexible retirement. In case of economic integration they both imply some capital outflow and may lead to some utility losses.
Classification-JEL: H2, F42, H8
Keywords: economic union, tax competition, social security
