Author-Name: DI SUMMA, Marco
Author-Email: disumma@math.unipd.it
Author-Workplace-Name: Dipartimento di Matematica, Università degli Studi di Padova, Italy
Title: The convex hull of the all-different system with the inclusion property: a simple proof
Abstract: An all-different constraint for a given family of discrete variables imposes the condition that no two variables in the family are allowed to take the same value. Magos et al. [Mathematical Programming, 132 (2012), pp. 209–260] gave a linear-inequality description of the convex hull of solutions to a system of all-different constraints, under a special assumption called inclusion property. The convex hull of solutions is in this case the intersection of the convex hulls of each of the all-different constraints of the system. We give a short and simple proof of this result, that in addition shows the total dual integrality of the linear system.
Classification-JEL: C10, C27
Keywords: all-different constraint, convex hull, integral polyhedron, total dual integrality
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 2013069
Creation-Date: 2013-12-31
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp2013.html
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:2013069

