Author-Name: MANIQUET, François
Author-Email: francois.maniquet@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, CORE, Belgium
Title: Social ordering functions
Abstract: We present the Fair Social Ordering approach to policy assessment. In an economic model, a Social Ordering Function (SOF) associates each economy in the domain with a complete ranking of the allocations. We describe the main achievements of the SOF theory. We present two applications, which show how SOF's can be used to evaluate policies. The first application concerns labor income taxation. The second application concerns the measurement of poverty. Finally, we discuss the relationship between the SOF approach and some other approaches to the construction of criteria to evaluate policies. 
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 2014051
Creation-Date: 2014-09-30
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp2014.html
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:2014051

Template-Type: ReDIF-Paper 1.0
Author-Name: EKELAND, Iver
Author-Workplace-Name: Université Paris-Dauphine
Author-Name: QUEYRANNE, Maurice
Author-Email: maurice.queyranne@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, CORE, Belgium
Title: Optimal pits and optimal transportation
Abstract: In open pit mining, one must dig a pit, that is, excavate the upper layers of ground before reaching the ore. The walls of the pit must satisfy some geomechanical constraints, in order not to collapse. The question then arises how to mine the ore optimally, that is, how to find the optimal pit. We set up the problem in a continuous (as opposed to discrete) framework, and we show, under weak assumptions, the existence of an optimum pit. For this, we formulate an optimal transportation problem, where the criterion is lower semi-continuous and is allowed to take the value +8. We show that this transportation problem is a strong dual to the optimum pit problem, and also yields optimality (complementarity slackness) conditions.
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 2014052
Creation-Date: 2014-10-31
File-URL: https://sites.uclouvain.be/core/publications/coredp/coredp2014.html
File-Format: application/pdf
Handle: RePEc:cor:louvco:2014052

