Author-Name: BELLEFLAMME, Paul 
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de Louvain, CORE, Belgium
Author-Name: TOULEMONDE, Eric
Title: Tax Incidence on Competing Two-Sided Platforms: Lucky Break or Double Jeopardy
Abstract: We consider the effects of taxes for competing two-sided platforms. We first detail how a platform passes a tax increase on its prices. Adding price competition, we study next how the tax affects profits. Because of the strategic implications of the cross-side external effects, the tax increase may end up increasing the profit of the taxed platform (lucky break) or, conversely, reducing it twice (double jeopardy).
Classification-JEL: D43, L13, L86, O32
Keywords: Two-sided platforms, taxation, pass-through
Series: UCLouvain, LIDAM, CORE
Number: 2016012
