Author-Name: GAO Zhengyuan, 
Author-Email: zhengyuan.gao@uclouvain.be
Author-Workplace-Name: Université catholique de louvain
Title: Uncertainty in economic growth and inequality
Abstract: A step to consilience, starting with a deconstruction of the causality of uncertainty that is embedded in the fundamentals of growth and inequality, following a construction of aggregation laws that disclose the invariance principle across heterogeneous individuals, ending with a reconstruction of metric models that yields deeper structural connections via U.S. GDP and income data.
Classification-JEL: C01, D01, E10
Keywords: abstract dynamical economy, infinite divisibility, aggregation, deep parameters, alpha and beta growth

